  "name": "two_node_two_sources",
  "description": "Two unknown nodes fed by a 20 V and a 10 V source: a standard two-equation nodal analysis exercise.",
  "derivation": "KCL at b (x20): 4(b-20) + 2b + 5(b-c) = 0, so 11b - 5c = 80. KCL at c (x12): 3(c-b) + 2c + 6(c-10) = 0, so -3b + 11c = 60. Determinant 121 - 15 = 106. b = (80*11 + 5*60)/106 = 590/53 V, c = (11*60 + 3*80)/106 = 450/53 V. Then I(R1) = (20-b)/5 = 94/53 A, I(R2) = b/10 = 59/53 A, I(R3) = (b-c)/4 = 35/53 A, I(R4) = c/6 = 75/53 A, I(R5) = (10-c)/2 = 40/53 A.",
